2026-09-27T10:24:37.8813947Z Update Note
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8814222Z ===========
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8814609Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8815001Z 
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8815118Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8815463Z ================
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8815882Z 
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8816296Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8816823Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8817147Z 
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8817309Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8817694Z ====================================
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8817949Z 
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8818145Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8818725Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8819264Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8820224Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8821089Z 
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8821234Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8821953Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8822812Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8823287Z 
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8823808Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8824499Z 
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8824638Z Packages
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8824929Z ========
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8825107Z 
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8827436Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8829785Z 
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8830138Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8830865Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8832072Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8833102Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8834046Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8834776Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8921448Z 
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8921640Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8922016Z ==========================
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8922280Z 
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8924091Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8926062Z 
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8927087Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8928392Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T10:24:37.8928709Z 
